# Local tooling artifacts
.memsearch/
.DS_Store

# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# `insta` writes these beside the committed `.snap` files when a snapshot test
# fails, so `cargo insta review` can show the diff. The accepted `.snap` is what
# belongs in git; a stray `.snap.new` committed next to it is a golden nobody
# agreed to.
**/*.snap.new

# `cargo run -p borbax-cli --release -- goldens --emit` writes these, and CI
# writes one per platform before diffing them. They are evidence produced by a
# run, not a reference checked into the tree — a stale one sitting in the repo
# would be read as authoritative by whoever found it next.
/goldens-*.txt

# Coverage instrumentation, if it is ever run.
*.profraw

# Task worktrees. `EnterWorktree` and the `superpowers:using-git-worktrees`
# fallback both place these here, so an unignored `.claude/worktrees/` shows up
# as untracked in the main checkout — and one `git add -A` from there commits an
# entire second copy of the repository into the repository. The worktree skill
# names that as its reason for requiring the directory be ignored *before* a
# worktree is created; it was not, from Task 3 until here.
.claude/worktrees/

# No Node section. This project is Rust-only by construction, and the web
# viewer was considered and rejected in spec §14.0 — ignoring node_modules
# would quietly imply the option is still open.
